00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.430
Dad, isn't this path...

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.890
Shh! Just walk.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.940
Th-This sound...!

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.480
It's the Azuki-Arai!

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:25.530
The Azuki-Babaa and Azuki-Hakari, too!

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.740
Run!

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:36.790
CHAPTER 31

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:41.710
AZUKI-ARAI, AZUKI-HAKARI, AZUKI-BABAA

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.960
Hey, eyes forward when you're walking.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.510
Aww.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.550
Huh? Was there a strange sound just now?

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.180
Hm? Was there?

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.050
Hello?

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:57.770
Oh, thank you so much for calling.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:01.600
Yes, we've been getting used to
the new offices.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.530
How's the water, Dad?

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.160
It's the perfect temperature.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.080
Ah, there you are.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.250
Say, Kitaro-chan,
I've got a juicy proposition for--

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.540
No thanks.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.250
I haven't said anything yet!

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.050
It's just some stupid
get-rich scheme, right?

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:29.050
<i>HOW TO BECOME A SUCCESSFUL OoTuber</i>

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.760
Looks like it.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:30.510
H-Hey!

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:34.390
You're always failing,
so why don't you give up already?

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:36.720
You've got no money-making sense.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.680
Sh-Shut up!

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:42.770
Like someone with that weird trinket
is one to talk about sense!

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:48.690
Don't you know? These days stuff like this
is called cute.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.240
I guess someone as old-fashioned
as you wouldn't understand.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:58.950
That damn Catchick,
running her mouth like that.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.040
I don't even have money for ramen.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.040
Isn't there some
exploitable chump anywhere?

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:08.500
Hey, chump!

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.550
Oh, it's just you three.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.390
Yeah, sorry it's just us.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.970
AZUKI-ARAI, AZUKI-HAKARI, AZUKI-BABAA

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.270
Nobody needs us anyway.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.390
Nobody...

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.940
Azuki...

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.860
Don't be so depressed.
You'll look gloomier than usual.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.820
You'd be gloomy too. We...

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.860
I get it.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.700
Kids these days don't even know
the sound of washing azuki beans,

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.870
so they don't notice you.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:47.830
All it took was a little azuki washing
and kids and adults used to run in fear...

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.550
The reason azuki beans have
faded in popularity

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.760
is because flashy Western sweets
came to our shores!

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.970
Those are the times. What can you do?

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:02.310
Isn't there some way we can remind
the humans of how good azuki beans are?

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.810
If so, I'm sure--

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:08.810
No way. Boring and weak <i>yokai</i> like you
aren't popular these--

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.570
Don't you know? These days stuff like this
is called cute.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.580
But, if you do as I say,
I might just have an idea.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.420
Did you bring the item?

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:32.380
Yeah. We use this "smartphone" thing to
take "videos", right?

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.050
Not just any videos. Fun, trendy videos
that'll make everyone envious.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.430
Well, that's no problem.
We recorded just the thing for that.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:43.810
Azuki!

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.140
Okay, show me what you got.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:53.900
Huh?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.360
Wait, is that all?

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.700
Get real!

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:05.450
This is just some withered old <i>yokai</i>
playing with azuki beans!

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.870
What's fun, trendy, and envious about it?!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.540
What?! What could be more fun
than washing azuki beans?

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:12.880
That's not fun!

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.420
Besides, there's no change in the angle.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.260
Yes, there's change!

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.970
Freshly picked azuki beans retain a sheen
and are still rough.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.180
They're like young lion cubs.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.770
By putting them in water--

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:27.770
Enough! Forget all that nonsense!

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.770
Listen. For now, forget azuki beans.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.770
Forget azuki beans...?!

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.690
You want azuki beans to be
popular again, right?

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:40.820
Then first you need to become
famous enough to be advertising pillars.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.030
Us? Famous?

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:48.250
If you promote azuki beans after that,
the day they reign supreme will come!

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.880
You forget azuki beans for now, adopt the
latest trends, and become popular.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:58.170
If it's for azuki beans...

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.260
Azuki...

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:04.220
But, even if it's only for now,
I can't forget azuki beans...

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:07.100
Don't you want azuki beans restored
to their former glory?

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.890
I do. But...

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:14.060
Don't worry. I'll be you guys' producer.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.240
Listen. You guys are going to become
famous OoTubers.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.120
Today is the first step.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:29.120
I don't get it.
Why are we dressed like this?

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.920
I've made you all look in the now
and youthful. Be thankful.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.170
Here's your order.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.460
Okay, here we go.

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.380
Let's begin filming.

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:42.050
Allow me to light it.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.810
What the hell is this?!

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.230
This is hopeless.

00:07:58.570 --> 00:07:59.480
<i>-"Not bad."
-"So extra. LOL"</i>

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.360
<i>"Too cute. LOL"</i>

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.320
Th-This is...!

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.500
Azuki!

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:17.880
SUBSCRIBERS

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:25.890
SUBSCRIBERS

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:29.890
SUBSCRIBERS

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:33.810
SUBSCRIBERS

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:43.030
And now, to our success...

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.400
-Cheers!
-Azuki!

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.330
Ahh, delicious!

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:53.660
The fact that we can drink such delicious
alcohol is all thanks to you three!

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.790
I never thought
things would go so smoothly.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.550
Your videos passed
a million views already.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:04.170
There's tons of merchandise
and you're well on the road to success!

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.590
Azuki!

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.260
I was right about you.

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:13.180
The moment I saw you,
I knew you all had the aura of a star.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:16.600
Sure, whatever you say.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:19.270
So, what about advertising azuki beans?

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.940
Can't we start doing that now?

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.950
Huh? Right, did we talk about that?

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:25.820
Oh!

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.950
Hello? This is BiBiBi Company.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.450
Yes, yes. Hello!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.500
Well, either way it's a wonderful night.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:38.420
Over the past few weeks
we've gained so much.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.880
Azuki.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.840
Is that really true?

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:46.010
I feel we've actually
lost something important.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:46.970
What?!

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.220
I haven't even touched
an azuki bean recently.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:55.350
All we've been doing is playing around
with human inventions.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.440
More and more it feels like
I'm losing the real me.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.230
Maybe our place is
with azuki beans after all.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.070
Is that the extent of
your azuki bean love?!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.030
This is all to restore azuki beans
to their former glory!

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:13.910
We have to abandon ourselves for now
and spread our names for that!

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:17.830
But, recently it's like you've forgotten
your original purpose

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:22.630
and are just enjoying
the humans fawning over you.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:25.130
Wh-Why you...!

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.890
Who's the one who doesn't really
love azuki beans, me or you two?!

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:33.390
-Why you little...!
-Azuki!

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.270
-Say that again!
-Wh-What are you doing?!

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.310
Why you...!

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:38.890
What's going on?

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.810
I'll be quitting as of today.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.820
Life's not worth it
if I can't weigh azuki beans!

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.900
What?! B-But...!

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:52.490
We're better off without
that wishy-washy twit!

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.330
Azuki-Babaa, from now on it's just us.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.040
Azuki...

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.090
<i>YOKAI</i> AZUKI-ARAI

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:08.590
<i>YOKAI</i> AZUKI-HAKARI

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:07.590
-<i>"No passing."</i>
-<i>"Ge."</i>

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:08.590
<i>"Look me in the eye and tell me."</i>

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.970
Rat Man and Azuki-Babaa are late.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:17.850
-It's almost time for the live stream.
-<i>Azuki!</i>

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:22.190
<i>A-zu-ki!</i>

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:23.190
Wh-...?!

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.190
Oh, it's Azuki Grandma!

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.070
What's that?

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:30.360
She was a famous OoTuber
who just made her solo singer debut.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:31.950
Huh.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.580
What's going on?!

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.250
No one told me anything!

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:45.500
Azuki.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.130
This is for azuki, too?!

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:50.880
Liar! You just want to be famous!

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.760
Hey! Let go!

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.640
Are you betraying me, too?!

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:05.900
Huh?

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.230
Rat Man.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:10.070
Azuki-Arai sensei, what's wrong?

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.740
Azuki-Babaa quit. She betrayed me...

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:17.990
<i>WEEKLY MAGAZINE
CURRENCY</i>

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:17.990
Hmm. Then I guess
you're done playing OoTuber.

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.700
Huh? What did you say?

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.920
You guys are useless unless you're a trio.

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.460
What can you do alone?

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:30.420
Besides, the money one makes producing
an OoTuber is peanuts.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:34.050
I better try my hand at
something more profitable.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:38.720
But, I thought we were going to
show the world the appeal of azuki beans!

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.430
Why the hell would I do that?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.390
Azuki beans won't sell in this age.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.150
So you were lying from the start?!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.400
Don't hold it against me.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.480
You got to dream a little, didn't you?

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.370
Why?

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:00.700
Why does everyone betray me?

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:04.920
I'll just have to do it myself then!

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.210
Hey, everyone! How are you?

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:10.170
-<i>"Welcome back."</i>
-<i>"Hey."</i>

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:11.050
-<i>"Selfie?"</i>
-<i>"Just you today?"</i>

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:13.550
I've got something
to share with you today.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:15.970
The wonderfulness of azuki beans!

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.180
-<i>"Huh?"</i>
-<i>"Azuki. LOL"</i>

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:17.970
<i>"Huh?"</i>

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:20.220
They're high in protein and low in fat!

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.310
Plus they've got lots of anthocyanin
so their antioxidative effect...

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:22.430
-<i>"A lecture??"</i>
-<i>"Something's off today."</i>

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.310
SUBSCRIBERS

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:27.270
L-Let's all eat more azuki beans!

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:32.030
<i>Osekihan</i> to celebrate!
<i>Manju</i> for Valentines!

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.030
-<i>"I don't get it."</i>
-<i>"Forget this..."</i>

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.070
SUBSCRIBERS

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.490
What...

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:43.830
What have I been doing all this time?

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:46.250
Where did I go wrong?

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:50.340
But, recently it's like you've forgotten
your original purpose

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:55.510
and are just enjoying
the humans fawning over you.

00:13:56.010 --> 00:14:00.100
Who's the one who doesn't really
love azuki beans, me or you two?!

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:02.430
No, no, no!

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:05.100
What? You're out of custard-filled ones?

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:07.980
I'm sorry. We have azuki paste ones.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:12.730
Hmm. Personally, azuki paste
doesn't hold up against custard.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.610
Dammit! Everyone talks down about
azuki beans.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:20.370
<i>Taiyaki</i> filling used to be
an azuki bean solo stage!

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.450
But because of flashy Western sweets...

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:28.960
If need be, I'll force the ignorant masses
to remember the greatness of azuki beans!

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:39.220
What a rare find!
Azuki-Arai, Azuki-Babaa, look at--

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.730
Thank you very much.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.990
Azuki?!

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.870
Take that, Western sweets!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.950
Take that, Western sweets!

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.250
Take that, Western sweets!

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:12.040
<i>This just in.</i>

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:14.500
<i>Currently, at sweets stores in the city,</i>

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:19.170
<i>strange cases are occurring of azuki bean
crops growing from people's faces.</i>

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:21.180
Hey, Kitaro.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:22.890
What is it, Catchick?

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:24.180
Look at this.

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:28.430
<i>It may be contagious. Please be careful
when going to sweets stores.</i>

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.980
Huh? Is that...

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.270
The Azuki-Arai?

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:32.860
Why is he doing this?

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:35.320
We won't learn anything here.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:37.820
We need to hurry and find the Azuki-Arai!

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:38.610
Right!

00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:44.280
The Azuki Allied Force lives around here.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:46.990
The Azuki-Arai might be hiding here.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:53.040
Hey, Azuki-Arai. Where are you?

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:57.380
Oh, Kitaro. Can I help you?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.300
We're looking for Azuki-Arai.

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:06.560
He's not here. Did he do something?

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:11.640
Azuki crops are growing on people's faces
in the city and it's causing a panic.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:13.900
Are you saying it's him?

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:18.190
I knew he was a fool, but not this much.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:21.030
If he's not here, we'll search the city.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:23.360
Will you come with us?

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.160
Why me?

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.660
Aren't you Azuki-Arai's friend?

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:31.290
Like hell I am. No way.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:32.540
Azuki-Hakari?

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:35.540
What's with him?

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:39.380
Hmm. We'll just have to go without him.

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:44.970
Take that, humans.

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:51.600
This is for forgetting Japan's taste
in sweets and drifting to Western sweets!

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:54.350
So this is your doing after all.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.440
Kitaro.

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:59.270
Azuki-Arai, why are you doing this?

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:02.240
Isn't it obvious?
It's all for azuki beans!

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.150
Azuki beans?

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:07.240
Without Western sweets,
the demand for azuki beans will rise!

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:11.160
Then people will remember
the greatness of azuki beans!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:15.250
Do you really think azuki beans will
become popular again that way?

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.170
Shut up!

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:23.510
Hair Needles.

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.480
Azuki-Hakari?

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:39.940
Why?

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:43.320
You idiot!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:48.200
Force-feeding azuki beans over
Western sweets won't gain them any glory.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:54.660
Even so, this is the only thing left
that I can do.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:59.290
You can't use azuki beans to cause pain.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:02.800
Azuki beans are for bringing joy.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.670
Isn't that right?!

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.340
Are you okay, Azuki-Hakari?

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.760
Do you still want to continue?

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.680
I made my choice.

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:16.890
That I'd restore azuki beans
to their former glory no matter what.

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.520
That's how I show my love for azuki beans!

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:27.030
<i>Azuki!</i>

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.700
<i>A-zu-ki!</i>

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.330
Azuki!

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:35.450
There! It's Azuki Grandma!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:37.830
Give me a <i>dorayaki</i>!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:39.420
A <i>manju</i> for me!

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:40.460
Azuki!

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.170
Is that Azuki-Babaa?

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:46.920
What's going on?

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:51.390
If you want Azuki Grandma merchandise,
you should line up right away.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.390
Merchandise...

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.140
At first I just bought them at concerts,

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:59.980
but Azuki Grandma's azuki beans are
all so delicious.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:02.940
Now these sweets are
one of the reasons to come.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:06.490
Yeah! I never realized azuki beans
tasted so good!

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:08.320
Could it be...

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.910
This is why she did her solo debut?

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:14.830
She didn't betray me after all?

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:18.960
I was hoping you'd trust me a little more.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.830
How many centuries have we been together?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.340
She talked?!

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:27.630
There's no need to dirty your hands
for azuki beans anymore.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:28.840
But...

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:33.180
It's all right.
Your love for azuki beans is genuine.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.230
We're the Azuki Allied Force.
We're friends.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:44.820
If one of us goes astray,
the other two will wake them up.

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:48.820
This time it just happened to be you.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:52.280
I didn't want to do what I did.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:55.280
But I didn't want to admit it.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:59.160
That I couldn't do anything
for azuki beans... That I was powerless...

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:03.670
Now that's enough with your crying.
Come help me sell azuki beans.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.590
Azuki-Hakari, Kitaro, will you help?

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.590
Uh... Sure.

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:11.630
EAT AND BE HAPPY
AZUKI DAY

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.890
Mister, could I have a custard-filled one?

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:19.730
We're out of custard,
but we do have azuki paste ones.

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.140
Again?!

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:24.190
Fine. Azuki paste will have to do today.

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:25.810
Thank you very much!

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:28.900
I've been on a sweets binge recently.

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.940
Here. You can have half.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.320
Thanks.

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:36.660
What is this?! It's delicious!

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:41.370
It's like the soft warm azuki paste
is melting in my mouth!

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.460
Thank you.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:46.000
Azuki paste isn't so bad.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:50.460
Actually, ever since we got new help,
our popularity has really risen.

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:54.380
Those three are really good at
handling azuki beans.

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:56.470
We're really counting on them.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.930
It really is delicious.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:03.520
Hey, let me have a bite.

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:04.690
Here.

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:08.070
It really is delicious.

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:10.440
<i>Salutations, Kitaro-sama.</i>

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:13.200
<i>Thank you so much for what you did.</i>

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:17.660
<i>Since then, azuki beans and Azuki-Babaa
became a smash hit,</i>

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:20.870
<i>but the fad ended in no time.</i>

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:24.460
<i>I no longer dream of restoring azuki beans
to their former glory.</i>

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:30.000
<i>Now I focus on washing azuki beans
and making those around me happy,</i>

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:32.840
<i>together with my precious friends.</i>

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:36.340
I've realized
that is what happiness is for me.

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.470
Hm? Did you say something?

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:39.720
Azuki?

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:43.100
Nope. Not a word.

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:47.100
Hold it, are you serious?!

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:52.070
The cryptocurrency I invested everything
into is worthless just like that?!

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:54.150
Are you Rat Man-san?

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:57.280
We've come to collect
what you've borrowed.

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:00.240
After him!

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:05.080
Where can I find a good chump?!

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.500
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.500
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.340
<i>"Hello" in the mountains</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.340
<i>yama de yahho</i>

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>If you call</i>

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>hitokoe yobeba</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>An identical "Hello"</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>onaji yahho</i>

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>The Yobuko calls back</i>

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>yobuko ga kaesu</i>

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>A tree spirit living in the mountains</i>

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>yama ni sunderu ki no seirei</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.860
<i>A used rag</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.860
<i>tsukatta zoukin</i>

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:35.740
<i>If you don't keep it clean</i>

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:35.740
<i>kirei ni shinaito</i>

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:38.110
<i>It'll get smelly</i>

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:38.110
<i>kusaku nattayo</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:43.490
<i>The Shiro-Uneri
Will tangle itself around you</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:43.490
<i>shirouneri karamitsuku</i>

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:46.040
<i>Stuck to your face
How horrible</i>

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:46.040
<i>kao ni bettori korya tamaran</i>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:51.540
<i>See how many ghosts there are</i>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:51.540
<i>konnani oruyo obaketachi</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.090
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.090
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:59.010
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:59.010
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:03.430
<i>They're near you</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:03.430
<i>kimi no chikaku ni</i>

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:09.060
<i>A legendary </i>yokai<i> sealed in Sakaiminato.</i>

00:23:09.190 --> 00:23:11.610
<i>Dad, now his power is...?!</i>

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:14.020
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:14.480 --> 00:23:17.070
<i>"Demon Belial
The Hundred-Year Grudge"</i>

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:19.610
<i>The door to the unseen world opens...</i>
